# Nothing in this repository is private: it IS the deployed static site, so every
# tracked file at or below the root is published by the host. A file added here is
# a file put on the public internet.
#
# A 6 MB archive, "Platform frontend review.zip", was tracked at the root from
# 2026-08-18 until 2026-09-01. It contained three complete Power Automate trigger
# URLs with intact sig= signatures — one of them the portal SUBMISSION endpoint the
# deployed config still uses. A signed trigger URL is a bearer credential: holding it
# is authorisation to invoke the flow. Removing the file does not revoke them; only
# regenerating the URLs in Power Automate does.
#
# Note that a text search of the tracked files finds nothing. The signatures were
# inside an archive, where grep cannot see them. Any scanner pointed at this
# repository has to read archive members.

# Credentials the operator creates locally. config.local.js carries every signed
# trigger URL the platform uses; it must never be committed.
config/config.local.js
config.local.js

# Archives. The estate has no reason to track one, and the last one carried
# credentials nobody could see.
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Local noise
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
